Bundled third-party source (PdfSharpCore)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

PdfSharpCore (https://github.com/ststeiger/PdfSharpCore, MIT-licensed) is
vendored into this repository under third_party/PdfSharpCore/ rather than
consumed as a NuGet package, so that PDF/A conformance fixes can be applied
at the source. Local modifications are marked with a "KillerPDF patch"
comment; see third_party/PdfSharpCore/VENDORED.txt for the upstream commit
and third_party/PdfSharpCore/LICENSE.md for its MIT license. The MIT license
and copyright notices are preserved intact.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Privacy / telemetry
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

TDPdf does not phone home by default. Released binaries ship with no
telemetry endpoint embedded. The OpenTelemetry pipeline is initialized at
startup but operates as a no-op unless an administrator has explicitly
provisioned an OTLP collector, either through the environment variables
TDPDF_OTLP_ENDPOINT and TDPDF_OTLP_TOKEN, or through policy values at:

    HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\TDPdf\Telemetry\OtlpEndpoint
    HKLM\SOFTWARE\Policies\TDPdf\Telemetry\OtlpToken

The policy key is ACL'd so that only SYSTEM and BuiltinAdministrators can
modify it. Reporting can be disabled on a device at any time with:

    TDPdf.exe /clear-telemetry

That writes a sentinel which outranks every configuration source above,
including administrator-pushed policy.

When provisioned, TDPdf emits usage events (App.Startup, Tool.Selected,
File.Open/New/Save/SaveFlattened/Merge/Split/Print, Install.Start/Success,
Install.Crash, Crash) to the configured collector. File paths, file names,
document content, user names, and persistent user identifiers are not
emitted. Stack traces are scrubbed of paths before transmission. Reports
carry the machine name (host.name); no other identifying field is sent,
and the per-launch session identifier is never stored. See PRIVACY.md and
docs/intune-distribution.md for full details.

Prior to version 1.24.0.0, TDPdf could also report to Azure Application
Insights, provisioned by a DPAPI-encrypted file at
%ProgramData%\TDPdf\telemetry.dat or by a build-time-embedded key. That
destination and both provisioning mechanisms have been removed; upgrading
deletes any telemetry.dat left behind.

